{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Seven days leaven shall not be found in your houses.</b> This verse comes to testify regarding 'on the first day you shall remove leaven from your houses,' which was said above — that the removal is not on the first day itself, but from before the day it is removed, for all seven days are equal; thus it is already removed from the eve of the festival. And there are those who say according to its plain sense: they need not have leaven found in their houses, for you are punished by excision for eating leaven, as it is written: 'for whoever eats what is leavened shall be cut off,' etc. <b>For whoever eats what is leavened.</b> We have heard the punishment; from where is the warning? The Talmud says: 'all leavened — you shall not eat.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:16.492851973Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}